ustible dust"}],"severe":false,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":null,"LFL_pct":13.1,"UFL_pct":21.7,"Tb_C":445},{"id":"N2","name":"Nitrogen","formula":"N2","cas":"7727-37-9","ghs":[{"code":"H280","text":"Contains gas under pressure; may explode if heated"},{"code":"ASPH","text":"Simple asphyxiant in confined spaces"}],"severe":false,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":null,"LFL_pct":null,"UFL_pct":23.5,"Tb_C":-196},{"id":"Ar","name":"Argon","formula":"Ar","cas":"7440-37-1","ghs":[{"code":"H280","text":"Contains gas under pressure; may explode if heated"},{"code":"ASPH","text":"Simple asphyxiant in confined spaces"}],"severe":false,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":null,"LFL_pct":null,"UFL_pct":23.5,"Tb_C":-186},{"id":"H2O","name":"Water","formula":"H2O","cas":"7732-18-5","ghs":[],"severe":false,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":null,"LFL_pct":null,"UFL_pct":23.5,"Tb_C":100}],"hazop":[{"node":"Sulphur furnace","deviation":"Sulphur fire or H2S in pit","cause":"Leaks, sulphur degassing","consequence":"SO2 release, H2S toxicity and explosion in the pit","safeguard":"Pit ventilation, H2S detectors, steam snuffing"},{"node":"Waste heat boiler","deviation":"Tube leak","cause":"Corrosion, low water level","consequence":"Water into SO3 gas makes acid, severe corrosion downstream","safeguard":"Level trips, conductivity monitoring"},{"node":"Converter","deviation":"High bed temperature","cause":"High SO2 strength","consequence":"Catalyst damage above 630 C, high emissions","safeguard":"SO2 analyser, bed thermocouples, furnace trip"},{"node":"Absorbers","deviation":"Low acid strength","cause":"Water dosing fault","consequence":"Acid mist from the stack, fast corrosion","safeguard":"Strength analysers, candle filters"},{"node":"Acid tanks and pumps","deviation":"Loss of containment","cause":"Corrosion, gasket failure","consequence":"Severe burns, reaction with water","safeguard":"Bunds, shields on flanges, PPE"}],"process_hazards":[{"hazard":"High temperature","detail":"Up to 1039 C. Creep, hydrogen attack and burns; refractory and tube skin temperature monitoring."},{"hazard":"Toxic materials","detail":"Sulphur dioxide. Toxic gas detection, emergency shutdown and isolation, escape sets, minimise inventory."},{"hazard":"Corrosive materials","detail":"Sulphur dioxide, Sulphur trioxide, Sulphuric acid. Material selection, PPE, safety showers, bunded storage."}],"validation":[{"metric":"Overall SO2 conversion, double absorption","model":99.942786,"published":[99.2,99.6],"unit":"%","error_pct":0.344162,"inside_range":false,"source":"ESA/Fertilizers Europe BAT Booklet No. 3 (2000), appendix A2: sulphur burning, double absorption","url":"https://www.fertilizerseurope.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Booklet_3_final.pdf","note":"Equilibrium beds give an upper bound; the booklet range is for plants of the late 1990s.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":1,"pass":true},{"metric":"Net energy export","model":3337.117819,"published":2500,"unit":"MJ/t","error_pct":33.484713,"inside_range":null,"source":"ESA/Fertilizers Europe BAT Booklet No. 3 (2000), appendix A2: net balance, sulphur burning","url":"https://www.fertilizerseurope.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Booklet_3_final.pdf","note":"Model counts 40 bar steam less blower and pump power; low grade absorber heat is not recovered. The same booklet puts 57 to 62% of the input heat into 31 bar steam (checked below), which is about 3,200 MJ/t on its own, so the 2,500 MJ/t net figure uses a basis the booklet does not state.","kind":"energy","tolerance_pct":25,"pass":false},{"metric":"Share of reaction heat recovered as HP steam","model":62.497323,"published":[57,62],"unit":"%","error_pct":0.802135,"inside_range":false,"source":"ESA/Fertilizers Europe BAT Booklet No. 3 (2000), appendix A8: Bayer 625 t/d plant, 31 bar steam","url":"https://www.fertilizerseurope.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Booklet_3_final.pdf","note":"Booklet basis: sulphur heat plus blower power in, 1.6% shell losses.","kind":"energy","tolerance_pct":5,"pass":true},{"metric":"Double absorption conversion (general statement)","model":99.942786,"published":[99.0,99.6],"unit":"%","error_pct":0.344162,"inside_range":false,"source":"ESA/Fertilizers Europe BAT Booklet No. 3 (2000), section 4: double absorption gives 99 to 99.6%","url":"https://www.fertilizerseurope.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Booklet_3_final.pdf","note":"","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":1,"pass":true}],"assumptions":["Each converter bed reaches equilibrium for SO2 + 1/2 O2 = SO3 evaluated 10 K above its adiabatic outlet temperature (ideal gas, components.json Gibbs data).","Furnace gas 11.0% SO2 (booklet sulphur burning range 6 to 12%). Air is dried to nil water; the removed water ends up in the product acid.","All gas cooling down to 180 C raises 40 bar 450 C steam, less the reheat of the interpass gas from 80 C. 3% of the steam is used to keep sulphur molten. Low grade absorber heat goes to cooling water.","SO3 is fully absorbed; the stack carries only the unconverted SO2.","Blower polytropic efficiency 0.80. Catalyst beds sized at a GHSV of 1,500 per h."],"notes":[]}